The HDR page of the video options: the row of HDR output in Advanced Video Options becomes a button
that shows the output (SDR..., HDR10..., scRGB...) and opens a page of its own, VideoHdrOptions:
the output to a display in HDR mode (d3d12_HDROutput, with a line of what the display is), the SDR
brightness (d3d12_HDRPaperWhite: Windows' or 80 to 480 nits), the peak brightness (d3d12_HDRPeak:
the display's or 250 to 4000 nits), the frame average limit (d3d12_HDRFrameAverage: Display or Off)
and, while the page is open, XRenderD3D12's test of the levels under them (d3d12_HDROutputDebug 3):
a square at 10000 nits around a smaller one at the peak, which disappears once the peak is the
display's, and patches at paper white, twice and four times that and at the peak. Its changes apply
at once and are saved when the page closes; back from it, what was chosen in Advanced Video Options
and not applied yet stays. Greyed out with another renderer. Written against VideoAdv.lua as
07-video-path-tracing.patch leaves it (Patch Scripts.cmd applies the patches in the order of their
numbers) and applied by Patch Scripts.cmd to FCData/Scripts.pak.

